From 131e73b759b7bdf0b7ddb0756783eaafbec53196 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 14:22:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] MFront: generic-parallel interface for behaviours

Integration of a behaviour over a batch of integration points, equivalent
to calling the generic interface at each point.

- Batch data described by fields with two strides (point by point or
  component by component storage), output status summarizing the batch.
- Per point integration written once in TFEL_HOST_DEVICE templates
  (MFront/GenericParallelBehaviour/Integrate.hxx); thin generated code.
- Backends: CUDA, HIP (one thread per point, reduction of the summary per
  warp, stack size increased if needed) and parallel algorithms of the
  C++ standard library (counting iterator).
- Same organisation as the generic-parallel interface for material
  properties: backend factory, options in configuration files, libraries
  suffixed by the backend.
